WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.381
Nello and Patrasche sat at the door of the hut.

2
00:00:05.382 --> 00:00:12.321
Across the village from the mill, Nello could hear the sounds of Alois' birthday.

3
00:00:12.322 --> 00:00:21.338
Little Alois was Nello's best friend, but her father had refused to invite him to her party.

4
00:00:21.339 --> 00:00:26.544
Nello was sad, but he turned his mind to other things.

5
00:00:26.545 --> 00:00:30.448
He looked at the little shed behind the hut.

6
00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:37.110
No one, except him, went in there, and inside was his great secret.

7
00:00:37.111 --> 00:00:40.590
Nello's secret was an easel.

8
00:00:40.591 --> 00:00:44.620
He had made it himself with pieces of wood.

9
00:00:44.621 --> 00:00:49.006
A large sheet of paper was attached to the easel.

10
00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:55.358
On the paper was a picture of an old man sitting on a fallen tree.

11
00:00:55.359 --> 00:00:59.232
The old man was Michel, the woodman.

12
00:00:59.233 --> 00:01:05.946
Nello had seen Michel many times, sitting alone on a log at dusk.

13
00:01:05.947 --> 00:01:08.674
The portrait was simple.

14
00:01:08.675 --> 00:01:13.447
It had a few small flaws, if you wanted to look for them.

15
00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:17.935
Yet it was very real and very beautiful.

16
00:01:17.936 --> 00:01:20.882
Nello had another secret:

17
00:01:20.883 --> 00:01:25.629
he planned to enter this portrait in an art competition.

18
00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:28.657
The competition was in Antwerp.

19
00:01:28.658 --> 00:01:33.017
It was open to anyone under eighteen years old.

20
00:01:33.018 --> 00:01:37.164
The prize was two hundred francs.

21
00:01:37.165 --> 00:01:43.758
All spring, summer, and autumn, Nello worked on his portrait of the woodman.

22
00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:50.700
When his milk deliveries were finished for the day, he crept into the shed to draw.

23
00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:58.530
He drew with charcoal, and many times, he went without food so that he could buy more charcoal.

24
00:01:58.531 --> 00:02:01.788
Nello said nothing to anyone.

25
00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:08.070
His grandfather would not have understood, and he did not see Alois anymore.

26
00:02:08.071 --> 00:02:11.083
He told only Patrasche.

27
00:02:11.084 --> 00:02:19.535
He whispered in the dog's ear, "The artist Rubens would give me first prize if he were the judge!"

28
00:02:19.536 --> 00:02:28.469
Patrasche agreed. Patrasche knew that Rubens had loved dogs because he had painted them so well.

29
00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:34.371
"People who love dogs are always good," Patrasche reasoned.

30
00:02:34.372 --> 00:02:39.035
The competition deadline was the first day of December.

31
00:02:39.036 --> 00:02:48.609
The prizes were to be announced on December 24 so that the winner could celebrate on Christmas Day.

32
00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:55.009
November 30, the day before the deadline, was a cold winter day.

33
00:02:55.010 --> 00:03:00.115
At twilight, Nello put his picture in the green milk cart.

34
00:03:00.116 --> 00:03:06.647
With Patrasche's help, they walked to Antwerp and through its dark streets.

35
00:03:06.648 --> 00:03:12.555
They found the large public building where the competition was being held.

36
00:03:12.556 --> 00:03:18.844
Nello nervously walked inside and set his picture on the table provided.

37
00:03:18.845 --> 00:03:22.214
"Perhaps it is worth nothing at all.

38
00:03:22.215 --> 00:03:25.637
How can I tell?" he thought.

39
00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:30.954
As Nello walked away, his heart beat fast.

40
00:03:30.955 --> 00:03:35.161
"Maybe it's a foolish idea," he thought.

41
00:03:35.162 --> 00:03:39.212
"I am just a poor boy who can barely read!

42
00:03:39.213 --> 00:03:44.361
Could I draw anything that a real artist might admire?"

43
00:03:44.362 --> 00:03:48.204
Nello and Patrasche passed the cathedral.

44
00:03:48.205 --> 00:03:53.450
There, Nello thought he saw the figure of Rubens in the fog.

45
00:03:53.451 --> 00:03:57.719
The figure seemed to say, "Have courage!

46
00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.660
I had to be brave to be a great painter.

47
00:04:01.661 --> 00:04:05.492
You can be too!"

48
00:04:05.493 --> 00:04:09.864
Nello ran home through the cold night, comforted.

49
00:04:09.865 --> 00:04:14.747
He had done his best, and he knew this was all he could do.

50
00:04:14.748 --> 00:04:25.017
Nello fell asleep, and Patrasche curled up next to him.

